LOCATION:Monroe County Public Library Southwest Branch\, 865 S Lora Batch
 elor Dr\, Bloomington\, IN 47403
SUMMARY:Reimagining Opera for Kids Presents: Ana y su sombra at Monroe Co
 unty Public Library-Southwest Branch
DESCRIPTION:Premiered Season 2013-14​Composed by Gabriela OrtizLibretto
  by Mónica Sánchez  ​  Performed by talented musicians from Reimagini
 ng Opera for Kids (https://www.reimaginingoperaforkids.org/) in partnersh
 ip with the Indiana University Center for Rural Engagement (https://www.r
 ural.indiana.edu) and the Jacobs School of Music (https://music.indiana.e
 du/index.html)\, this engaging show features music sung in Spanish with s
 poken English narration\, making the story accessible\, interactive\, and
  fun for audiences of all ages.  ANA Y SU SOMBRA follows the story of a y
 oung girl\, Ana\, who is the daughter of diplomats to the United States. 
 Out of terrible homesickness for Mexico\, she hides herself away - howeve
 r\, her shadow wants to explore and participate in the world where they a
 re living. The two part ways over this disagreement\, and ultimately disc
 over whether they can live separately or must reconcile.Appropriate for y
 oung audiences and families | Sung in Spanish\, with English narration​
 Performance length: approx. 30 minutes
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong><em>Premiered Season 2013-14</em>
 </strong><br /><strong><em>​Composed by Gabriela Ortiz</em></strong><br
  /><strong><em>Libretto by Mónica Sánchez</em></strong><br />  ​<br /
 >  Performed by talented musicians from <a href="https://www.reimaginingo
 peraforkids.org/">Reimagining Opera for Kids</a> in partnership with the 
 Indiana University <a href="https://www.rural.indiana.edu" target="_blank
 " rel="noopener">Center for Rural Engagement</a> and the <a href="https:/
 /music.indiana.edu/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jacobs Scho
 ol of Music</a>\, this engaging show features music sung in Spanish with 
 spoken English narration\, making the story accessible\, interactive\, an
 d fun for audiences of all ages.</p><hr /><p>  ANA Y SU SOMBRA follows th
 e story of a young girl\, Ana\, who is the daughter of diplomats to the U
 nited States. Out of terrible homesickness for Mexico\, she hides herself
  away - however\, her shadow wants to explore and participate in the worl
 d where they are living. The two part ways over this disagreement\, and u
 ltimately discover whether they can live separately or must reconcile.</p
 ><p><strong>Appropriate for young audiences and families | Sung in Spanis
 h\, with English narration</strong><br /><strong>​Performance length: a
 pprox. 30 minutes</strong></p>
