SUMMARY:Brent Wallarab Jazz Ensemble
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy this performance from almost anywhere in the world viaL
 IVE@jacobs!About the DirectorBrent Wallarab\, composer\, arranger\, produ
 cer\, and educator\, has a career spanning nearly five decades. The Busel
 li-Wallarab Jazz Orchestra\, founded in 1994 with trumpeter and educator 
 Mark Buselli\, held a 12-plus-year weekly residency at Indianapolis' fame
 d Jazz Kitchen and has produced nine albums\, including 2023's award-winn
 ing album The Gennett Suite. Since 2004\, Wallarab has been arranger for 
 the American Pianists Association\, writing commissions in collaboration 
 with pianists Emmet Cohen\, Kenny Banks Jr.\, Sullivan Fortner\, Isaiah J
 . Thomas\, Paul Cornish\, Aaron Diehl\, Dan Tepfer\, and many others. In 
 2025\, Wallarab was arranger\, conductor\, and producer of Stryker with S
 trings – Goes to the Movies with guitarist Dave Stryker. The album rema
 ined in the top five of the jazz charts for 14 weeks. Wallarab was musica
 l director and arranger for the 2024 Emmy Award winning PBS special Wes M
 ontgomery at 100 and was nominated for an Emmy for the 2017 PBS productio
 n of his work The Gennett Suite. Wallarab is The David N. Baker Professor
  of Music in Jazz Studies at the Indiana University Jacobs School of Musi
 c. He was inducted into the Indianapolis Jazz Hall of Fame in 2017 and is
  an active member of the Recording Academy (Grammy Awards).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Enjoy this performance from almos
 t anywhere in the world via</strong><a href="https://liveatjacobs.music.i
 ndiana.edu/"><strong>LIVE@jacobs</strong></a><strong>!<br /></strong></p>
 <p><strong>About the Director</strong><br /><br /><strong>Brent Wallarab<
 /strong>\, composer\, arranger\, producer\, and educator\, has a career s
 panning nearly five decades. The Buselli-Wallarab Jazz Orchestra\, founde
 d in 1994 with trumpeter and educator Mark Buselli\, held a 12-plus-year 
 weekly residency at Indianapolis' famed Jazz Kitchen and has produced nin
 e albums\, including 2023's award-winning album <em>The Gennett Suite.</e
 m> Since 2004\, Wallarab has been arranger for the American Pianists Asso
 ciation\, writing commissions in collaboration with pianists Emmet Cohen\
 , Kenny Banks Jr.\, Sullivan Fortner\, Isaiah J. Thomas\, Paul Cornish\, 
 Aaron Diehl\, Dan Tepfer\, and many others. In 2025\, Wallarab was arrang
 er\, conductor\, and producer of <em>Stryker with Strings – Goes to the
  Movies</em> with guitarist Dave Stryker. The album remained in the top f
 ive of the jazz charts for 14 weeks. Wallarab was musical director and ar
 ranger for the 2024 Emmy Award winning PBS special <em>Wes Montgomery at 
 100</em> and was nominated for an Emmy for the 2017 PBS production of his
  work <em>The Gennett Suite.</em> Wallarab is The David N. Baker Professo
 r of Music in Jazz Studies at the Indiana University Jacobs School of Mus
 ic. He was inducted into the Indianapolis Jazz Hall of Fame in 2017 and i
 s an active member of the Recording Academy (Grammy Awards).</p>
