SUMMARY:A Well-Advised Lunch with Lisa Hasson
DESCRIPTION:Hasson currently serves as Chorus Master and Apprentice Artis
 t Program Director at Des Moines Metro Opera\, as well as an opera facult
 y member at the Cincinnati College-Conservatory of Music. Praised for her
  opera chorus direction\, coaching\, and administrative expertise\, Hasso
 n brings a unique perspective on building and sustaining a career in the 
 classical music industry. Students will gain practical insight into makin
 g themselves more competitive for opera chorus opportunities\, strengthen
 ing their résumés\, navigating the transition from a master's degree in
 to the profession\, and maintaining an active opera career while balancin
 g supplemental income. Whether you're preparing for auditions\, looking t
 o workshop your résumé\, or wondering how to build a sustainable career
  after graduation\, this riveting conversation is not to be missed!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Hasson currently serves as Chorus Maste
 r and Apprentice Artist Program Director at Des Moines Metro Opera\, as w
 ell as an opera faculty member at the Cincinnati College-Conservatory of 
 Music. Praised for her opera chorus direction\, coaching\, and administra
 tive expertise\, Hasson brings a unique perspective on building and susta
 ining a career in the classical music industry. Students will gain practi
 cal insight into making themselves more competitive for opera chorus oppo
 rtunities\, strengthening their résumés\, navigating the transition fro
 m a master's degree into the profession\, and maintaining an active opera
  career while balancing supplemental income. Whether you're preparing for
  auditions\, looking to workshop your résumé\, or wondering how to buil
 d a sustainable career after graduation\, this riveting conversation is n
 ot to be missed!</p>
