DESCRIPTION:Featuring  Eric Bowling\, flute (alumnus guest)  Jacob Burk\,
  violaSara Dailey\, narrator (alumna guest)&#160\;Helen Ford\, cello (gue
 st)  Michael Grubb\, narrator (guest)  Maria Izzo\, soprano (alumna guest
 )  Emily Nehus\, violin (alumna guest)  Paulina Villarreal\, mezzo-sopran
 o/narrator  RepertoireChappell Kingsland: Confessions of a Murderess (201
 1)Anthony Plog: Animal Ditties I (1978)Daniel Cueto: Ave (2025)Elaine Fin
 e: Happy Family (2005)Jenni Brandon: The Woman with the Unfathomable Eyes
  (2010)About the Artists  Clarinetist Mike Mattner (M.M. University of Co
 lorado\, Boulder\; B.Mus.Ed. Crane School of Music-SUNY Potsdam) has enjo
 yed a teaching and performing career spanning 34 years. He is a former me
 mber of the Midland Symphony\, Boulder MahlerFest Orchestra\, Philharmoni
 a à Vent\, Orion Winds\, Bloomington Pops\, Bloomington Symphony\, Class
  Act Productions\, Houston Repertoire Ballet\, The Woodlands Concert Band
 \, and the Woodland Winds Quintet\, and has performed in numerous musical
  theater productions. He currently performs with the Bloomington Symphony
  Orchestra\, the Southern Indiana Wind Ensemble\, Reimagining Opera for K
 ids\, Voces Novae\, and several chamber music ensembles.Kimberly Carballo
  serves in the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music as Director of J
 acobs Virtual Academy (JVA) and as teaching professor in the Chamber Musi
 c and Collaborative Piano department. Carballo is also an active internat
 ional performer and educator\, teaching both at the university and in her
  private studio. She is a strong believer in and practicer of community e
 ngagement locally and globally. She founded Reimagining Opera for Kids (R
 OK)\, a music Bloomington-based community engagement and education progra
 m\, participates annually as faculty advisor for the IU portion of the te
 am in the Cheerful Heart Music Education Mission in the Dominican Republi
 c and Haiti\, and is a founding member of the Amity Trio\, a chamber ense
 mble that commissions and performs new music to amplify underrepresented 
 voices.
